morning, class" said Mr.

2
00:00:10.274 --> 00:00:13.156
Aron. "Today we have a visitor."

3
00:00:15.698 --> 00:00:16.378
Jada looked up.

4
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.142
The visitor was Miss Santiago, the school nurse.

5
00:00:28.007 --> 00:00:28.847
somebody sick?"

6
00:00:29.247 --> 00:00:29.748
asked Paul.

7
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.121
The nurse smiled and shook her head.

8
00:00:33.141 --> 00:00:36.945
"I'm here to talk about food allergies."

9
00:00:39.787 --> 00:00:42.029
"Ooh!" Mike waved his arm.

10
00:00:42.049 --> 00:00:45.051
"I'm allergic to peanuts!"

11
00:00:48.574 --> 00:00:50.616
"I'm allergic to shrimp," said Matt.

12
00:00:50.636 --> 00:00:55.400
"I can't eat eggs," said Jennifer.

13
00:00:55.420 --> 00:01:01.557
"My sister is allergic to tree nuts," said Jada.

14
00:01:05.119 --> 00:01:07.481
"What happens if you eat these things?"

15
00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.082
asked Miss Santiago.

16
00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:13.485
"I get a bad stomachache," said Matt.

17
00:01:13.505 --> 00:01:17.929
"Then I throw up!"

18
00:01:17.949 --> 00:01:21.972
"I get itchy," said Jennifer.

19
00:01:29.144 --> 00:01:31.246
"Are food allegies dangerous?"

20
00:01:31.746 --> 00:01:32.467
asked Carly.

21
00:01:32.487 --> 00:01:36.670
"They can be dangerous," said the nurse.

22
00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:40.413
"Some kids have severe allergies.

23
00:01:41.614 --> 00:01:43.295
Foods can stop their breathing.

24
00:01:44.536 --> 00:01:46.158
But there's medicine to help."

25
00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.261
Jennifer raised her hand.

26
00:01:50.281 --> 00:01:54.464
"If you're allergic to foods, what can you do?"

27
00:01:54.484 --> 00:01:58.928
"Good question, Jennifer," said Miss Santiago.

28
00:02:00.072 --> 00:02:01.332
"Anyone have an idea?

29
00:02:01.893 --> 00:02:03.713
How can you protect yourself?"

30
00:02:03.733 --> 00:02:09.215
"Always check food labels," said Carly.

31
00:02:09.235 --> 00:02:14.596
"Don't trade food with other kids," said Mike.

32
00:02:19.998 --> 00:02:22.278
your allergy medicine everywhere!"

33
00:02:22.658 --> 00:02:23.199
said Jada.

34
00:02:23.219 --> 00:02:26.460
"Great ideas!"

35
00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:27.840
said Miss Santiago.

36
00:02:29.088 --> 00:02:30.769
"You must also speak up.

37
00:02:33.612 --> 00:02:34.993
Tell teachers and friends.

38
00:02:36.034 --> 00:02:38.656
Make sure everyone knows about your allergy.

39
00:02:45.081 --> 00:02:46.662
That will keep you healthy."

40
00:02:48.283 --> 00:02:49.444
Paul raised his hand.

41
00:02:49.464 --> 00:02:52.266
"I have a severe allergy.

42
00:02:52.827 --> 00:02:54.388
But it's not a food allergy."

43
00:02:58.248 --> 00:02:59.210
"What is it then, Paul?"

44
00:02:59.751 --> 00:03:00.271
asked Mr.

45
00:03:00.392 --> 00:03:03.036
Aron. Paul grinned.

46
00:03:09.445 --> 00:03:10.928
I'm allergic to homework!"
